  "description": "Organizations use information systems to track, control, and steward their resources and their relationships with stakeholders, whether by keeping records, analyzing past performance, or predicting future performance. Therefore, information systems are relevant to most organizational functions. The information systems minor familiarizes students with relevant fundamentals in business and computing, so that in their future callings they may collaborate more effectively with technologists. Overlap Policy This program may not be combined with the business analytics, BS, program. No more than two minors from the School of Business may be obtained.",
